title: Choosing one of four
mode: vhdl
chapter: Buses and numbers
check: behaves
---- intro
`with ... select` can choose a signal, not only a constant. A 2-bit select `s` picks one of the four bits of `d`:

| s | y |
|---|---|
| 00 | `d(0)` |
| 01 | `d(1)` |
| 10 | `d(2)` |
| 11 | `d(3)` |

The last case is usually written `when others`, which covers anything left.
---- task
Make `y` the bit of `d` that `s` points at.
---- start
library ieee;
use ieee.std_logic_1164.all;

entity mux4 is
  port(
    d : in  std_logic_vector(3 downto 0);
    s : in  std_logic_vector(1 downto 0);
    y : out std_logic
  );
end mux4;

architecture rtl of mux4 is
begin
    -- write it here
end rtl;
---- answer
library ieee;
use ieee.std_logic_1164.all;

entity mux4 is
  port(
    d : in  std_logic_vector(3 downto 0);
    s : in  std_logic_vector(1 downto 0);
    y : out std_logic
  );
end mux4;

architecture rtl of mux4 is
begin
    with s select y <=
        d(0) when "00",
        d(1) when "01",
        d(2) when "10",
        d(3) when others;
end rtl;
---- hint1
Four cases, like the decoder, but each gives a bit of `d` instead of a constant.
---- hint2
`with s select y <= d(0) when "00", d(1) when "01", d(2) when "10", d(3) when others;`
---- solution
```
with s select y <=
    d(0) when "00",
    d(1) when "01",
    d(2) when "10",
    d(3) when others;
```
---- done
A processor picks one of its 32 registers to read with a multiplexer like this, 32 inputs wide.
